# Normalise line endings.
#
# core.autocrlf gives the working tree CRLF on Windows while git stores LF. That is mostly
# harmless until a check reads the working tree rather than the index: .editorconfig declares
# LF, so on a platform that checks out CRLF, `dotnet format --verify-no-changes` fails on a
# fresh clone nobody has edited. Forcing LF in the working tree makes local checks and CI
# agree on every platform.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, never translated.
*.ico binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
